{
  "$comment": [
    "What scripts/site-crops.mjs cuts out of the captures, and how. Run it with --sources <folder>.",
    "The captures are real sessions of the app, 2560 x 1440 px: a 1280 x 720 window at scale 2 (HANGAR_DEV_CAPTURE_DIR, see shell/dev_screenshot.rs).",
    "rect: [x, y, width, height] in capture pixels (scale 1: one capture pixel per unit),",
    "or { \"ref\": \"path/in/the/rects/index\" } with optional pad and x/y/w/h overrides.",
    "In a list of the index, a path step is a position or an entry's name: stills/en/hero/rects/workers/Zoe/box.",
    "widths: the files written, img/<name>-<width>.avif and .webp; the page's srcset follows them.",
    "fade: pixels over which an edge the crop cuts through fades to that edge's own colour.",
    "Names ending in -m are the phone crops: one panel, drawn near its real size on a phone.",
    "Names starting with mobile- are Hangar Mobile itself, in its mock mode (pnpm mobile:dev): whole screens,",
    "390 x 844 at scale 2 with an iPhone's safe areas, the PC and the workspace renamed; the page draws the phone."
  ],
  "scale": 1,
  "out": ".",
  "href": "img/",
  "page": "../index.html",
